---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Delete Lullaby Data"
  description="How to delete all locally stored Lullaby data."
>
  <article class="reading">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>Delete Lullaby data</h1>
      <p class="post-desc">There is no account or server copy.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>
        Lullaby's first release stores information only on your Android device.
        Pastello Club does not hold an account or cloud copy to delete.
      </p>

      <h2>Delete from inside Lullaby</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
        <li>Open <strong>Local data & privacy</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Delete all local data</strong>.</li>
        <li>Confirm <strong>Delete everything</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Delete through Android</h2>
      <p>
        Android Settings → Apps → Lullaby → Storage → Clear storage also removes
        the app's local information. Uninstalling the app removes its private
        local storage.
      </p>

      <p>
        Deletion is permanent because this release has no cloud backup. Export a
        copy first if you need one.
      </p>

      <p>
        Need help? Email
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Lullaby data deletion`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        {' '}without attaching sensitive baby information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
